WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.500
- Lionel Hutz is unstoppable,

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.530
and the best part is,

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.900
if you don't win your
case, your pizza is free.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.140
- You'd be surprised how often that works.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.180
You really would.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.559
- So contrary to popular
belief, Lionel Hutz, A tier.

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:15.059
(light music)

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.280
Well, it's finally happening.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.450
Today, we are going to rank

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.750
all of the fictional lawyers on TV.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.360
Now, usually when you see
these sort of tier rankings,

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.000
they're people's opinions, but
that is not the case today.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.500
These are absolutely
true as a matter of law,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.300
because of course I have
the power of attorney.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.180
The power of attorney!

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.260
Though, at the same time, I
have no idea what I'm doing.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.100
If only there were some
sort of YouTube channel

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.733
that specialized in tier
rankings that could lend a hand.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.630
- I might be able to help with that.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.980
- Oh, Tier Zoo.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.090
What are you doing here?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.960
Got any tips on how I should rank

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.800
all of these fictional TV lawyers?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.480
- Tier lists are best used to
compare characters in games

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.490
where each character has
a unique set of abilities

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.280
and a lot of variation in their stats.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.130
Attributes like mobility,
raw power and defense

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.380
heavily influenced how well
a character can match up

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.800
against the rest of the game's roster.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.890
The devs designed the characters

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.020
to hopefully be fairly equal in viability,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.060
but the best players will
still naturally gravitate

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.300
towards the characters that
have advantages where it counts.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.960
Those characters, called top tiers,

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.780
are gonna comprise your A and S tier.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.100
Characters that have a lot of potential,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.110
but maybe have one or
two major weaknesses,

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.610
are gonna take up your middle tiers,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.880
as will the sort of Jack
of all trades characters.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:23.910
And in the bottom tiers,

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:24.930
that's where you'd find the characters

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.230
that nobody in their right
mind would play competitively,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.250
usually because they're
hugely lacking in power

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.260
or have a massively exploitable
flaw in their strategy.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.700
- Yeah, I'm not sure that
that entirely applies

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.450
in this particular
case, but what the heck?

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.440
Let's give it a try.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.250
- Sorry man, I don't make the rules.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.930
- Well, thank you for
stopping by, Tier Zoo.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.150
So today we're ranking
fictional TV lawyers

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.970
and we'll be doing that
using several criteria.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.260
First of all, law skills.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.260
Self-explanatory, we're ranking lawyers.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.950
Second of all, fighting ability.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.310
This includes, of course,
intelligence, power, defense,

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.250
mobility, vitality, and stealth.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.530
And then finally third,

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.480
do they have any sort of special ability

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.710
that would give them an advantage

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.010
in or outside of the courtroom?

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.400
All right, with the rules established,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.253
let's get in and rank these lawyers.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.700
Phoenix Wright, a longtime favorite

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.210
of viewers of this channel.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.720
Recent law grad, high fighting ability,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.370
seems to have reasonable intelligence,

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.860
seems to be reasonably fit.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.620
The problem is his law
skills are extremely,

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.453
extremely lacking.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.770
- [Phoenix] Objection!

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.990
- Being a new recent law grad,

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.450
it seems like there's almost
someone else controlling him,

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.480
telling him what to do

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.630
because he has absolutely
no idea what he's doing.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.270
He's often told what the evidence is

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.590
by witnesses to the case,

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.230
has no comprehension of
the rules of evidence,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.930
and is a terrible trial lawyer.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.040
He's even been accused of murder himself.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.350
Though special abilities
do include bike riding

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.780
and excellent hair,

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.100
though this is not enough
to save Phoenix Wright

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.720
from absolute F tier, garbage.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:50.553
Ace attorney?

00:02:50.553 --> 00:02:52.660
More like (beep) attorney.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:53.709
- Monster.

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:56.626
(video game music)

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:00.560
- Theodore Ted Bucklin
from the TV show "Scrubs",

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.630
the in-house lawyer for
the hospital Sacred Heart.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.330
Actually, lawyer skills
were not too too bad,

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.370
middle of the pack here.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.220
Often gave reasonably
good advice to the doctors

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.690
and administrators of Sacred Heart.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.090
- If you know about something,

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.590
by not reporting, it you're
every bit as culpable.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.610
Now is there anything you wanna tell me?

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.220
- Unfortunately, no one ever
ever followed Ted's advice.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.990
Known as the hospital sad sack,

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.330
you're only as good as your
ability to get your clients

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.290
to actually follow your advice,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.750
and Ted was simply
never able to get anyone

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.610
to follow any of his advice.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.630
Though special abilities
include flop sweat.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.000
- Ted, you ready to get started?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.500
- Whenever you're ready, Nina.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.040
- His ability to basically
be invisible at all times,

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.475
and of course his ability
to sing like an angel.

00:03:46.475 --> 00:03:50.142
♪ When you wish upon a star ♪

00:03:51.557 --> 00:03:52.500
RIP Sam Lloyd,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.940
and one of my favorite portrayals
of any lawyer on TV ever

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.199
not withstanding, D tier.

00:03:58.199 --> 00:04:01.340
(video game music)

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.300
Bob Loblaw from "Arrested Development".

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.090
Bob Loblaw needs no introduction,

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.670
especially with respect
to Bob Loblaw's law blog.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.830
- Of course, the Bob Loblaw law blog.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.260
Wow, you sir are a mouthful.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.820
- He can do anything that
Barry Zuckerkorn can do,

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.070
plus skew younger.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.820
He gets extremely high materia

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.650
from the fact that he's able to bill

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.190
out of just about everything.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.670
- Why should you go to jail

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.930
for a crime someone else noticed?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.880
- Still, his lawyering skills themselves

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.470
are a little bit underwhelming.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.303
C tier.

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.998
(video game music)

00:04:34.998 --> 00:04:37.630
Maggie Lizer from "Arrested Development".

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.250
Known as one of the most feared
attorneys in Orange County,

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.630
being able to navigate the
legal waters in Orange County,

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.930
despite her apparent blindness.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.490
But of course she wasn't actually blind.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.320
- I submit into evidence this wine glass

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.226
with the defendant's fingerprints.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.059
(glass breaking)

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:55.190
- This gambit gave her high stealth,

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.230
but very, very poor mobility,

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.560
especially given the fact
that her special ability,

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:03.120
her seeing eye dog Justice,
actually happened to be blind.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.216
In this case, no avoiding F tier lawyer.

00:05:06.216 --> 00:05:09.529
(video game music)

00:05:09.529 --> 00:05:13.530
Eli Stone from the
eponymous TV show on ABC.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.440
I didn't really see this one,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:18.240
and apparently no one
else saw this either.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.330
Has a good last name.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.560
Lawyering skills were apparently okay,

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.310
though his special ability
did include hallucinations,

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.680
which is actually a bit of
a nerf in and of itself.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.797
- Are you God?

00:05:28.797 --> 00:05:31.150
- Well, someone has said so.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:33.514
- [Devin] So, I don't know, D tier?

00:05:33.514 --> 00:05:36.431
(video game music)

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.990
Saul Goodman slash Jimmy McGill

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.550
from "Breaking Bad"
and "Better Call Saul".

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:42.860
- Hi, I'm Saul Goodman.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.380
Did you know that you have rights?

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:48.410
- Here, Jimmy slash Saul's
lawyering abilities are top-notch

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.060
despite not going to a top law school.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.310
- The University of American Samoa.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.810
Go Land Crabs!

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.530
- He is able to dig in when he is willing

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.270
to put in the time and the
effort to get the results,

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.050
and his knowledge of civil procedure

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.800
and just interpersonal relationships

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.410
is absolutely top notch.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.614
And later in the game,

00:06:06.614 --> 00:06:09.550
Saul gets access to one
of the best partners

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.510
in the entire build, Huell.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:15.520
Though because Jimmy is so
absolutely unscrupulous,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.210
that does knock him down a peg.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:21.458
So close to getting S tier,
but easily makes A tier.

00:06:21.458 --> 00:06:24.982
(video game music)

00:06:24.982 --> 00:06:27.470
Barry Zuckerkorn from
"Arrested Development".

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.530
Perhaps the worst law
skills of any attorney

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.170
on this entire list.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.410
There's a reason why the Bluths

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.702
have just the worst (beep) attorneys.

00:06:36.702 --> 00:06:39.180
- I got the worst (beep) attorneys.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:42.950
- And Barry Zuckerkorn is
absolutely no exception here.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.740
- I had a really
interesting date last night,

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:49.133
a woman who actually works two jobs.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:51.740
- He doesn't read contracts.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.500
He gives terrible, terrible legal advice.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.600
He does have a special ability
and that is dance management,

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.500
but because he is more interested
in running a dance studio

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.568
than he is actually
practicing law, F tier.

00:07:03.568 --> 00:07:07.158
(video game music)

00:07:07.158 --> 00:07:09.670
Annalise Keating from "How
To Get Away With Murder".

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.480
I covered the show in
a Real Lawyer Reacts.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:14.330
Honestly, it almost caused me an aneurysm.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.370
- [Keating] I lied.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.420
This isn't a past case,

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:19.140
but when I took last
week after Gina fired...

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.040
- Wait, are there law students there?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.760
The show is ridiculous, and
the character Annalise Keating,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.420
I don't think actually knows
anything about the law,

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.850
despite the fact that she
is a putative law professor.

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.480
But she makes up for her terrible

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.876
or non-existent lawyering skills

00:07:33.876 --> 00:07:37.240
with a special ability group attack.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.600
She basically just corrals
all of her law students

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.930
to fight for her, leading
to the interesting tech

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.400
of Group Cyclone.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.160
- This is not an advanced
trial skills class.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.450
In fact, this is not a class at all.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.360
This is a sacrifice.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.520
- Also, let's just say
she has rocket punch.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:55.883
Absolute D tier trash.

00:07:56.821 --> 00:08:00.200
(video game music)

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.350
Harvey Specter, and
Mike Ross from "Suits".

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.280
These guys are all over the map.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:07.830
Harvey Specter is known as the
best closer at the law firm.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.840
- I'm not just a lawyer to Jerome, okay?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.340
I'm, I'm more like Robert
Duvall in "The Godfather".

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.450
- But he is almost never able
to actually close things.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:20.530
His actual legal skills in
the courtroom are subpar.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:24.540
He likes to bluster without
actually knowing when to object,

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.340
rarely makes the right objection,
makes speaking objections,

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:30.390
and is just an okay at best trial lawyer.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.420
Mike Ross, on the other
hand, is supposed to be

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.950
this God-like attorney.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.710
He has a photographic memory,

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.350
but the thing is, a photographic memory

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.840
doesn't actually help you as an attorney.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.270
As we saw from some of
the very first episodes,

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.110
despite the fact that he
could remember things,

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.660
he didn't actually know the
things in the first place

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.550
when it came to actually litigating.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:52.580
- Usually, the trial
starts and there's a judge,

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.330
and then people say things.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.640
- You've never done this before, have you?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.060
- He needed help from the paralegals.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.300
He didn't know anything
about legal research,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.170
which is what most lawyers do,

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.313
and he isn't great at brief writing.

00:09:05.721 --> 00:09:06.554
(Devin sighs)

00:09:06.554 --> 00:09:08.533
These guys, ah, B tier.

00:09:09.383 --> 00:09:13.060
(video game music)

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:15.810
The Unfrozen Caveman lawyer
from "Saturday Night Live".

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:18.690
Lawyer Key Rock was a caveman.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.730
He was frozen during the ice age

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.620
and scientists were able to thaw him out.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.650
As a result, he's a
stranger in a strange land,

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:28.150
and he's confused by
our modern accoutrement.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.393
- Your world frightens and confuses me.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:35.361
Sometimes the honking
horns of your traffic

00:09:35.361 --> 00:09:39.210
make me want to get out of my BMW.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.480
- He uses that to great advantage.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.730
His special ability is,
of course, confusion.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.730
He uses that confusion, or
"confusion", If you will,

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:50.179
to confuse the jury into
basically finding for his clients

00:09:50.179 --> 00:09:53.360
in every single trial
he's ever participated in.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.650
Despite his appearance,
extremely high intelligence,

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.980
leading to great fighting ability,

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.110
though he does have pretty
low vitality as a result of,

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.950
you know, frankly, being frozen.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.550
And one of two lawyers on this list

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.630
portrayed by Phil Hartman.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.107
Actually, not to spoil anything,

00:10:07.107 --> 00:10:10.370
but I'm not sure the character
voiced by Phil Hartman

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.320
has ever lost a trial.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.200
But in particular, the
Unfrozen Caveman lawyer

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.670
uses his personal history
to the best of effect,

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.030
never losing a trial.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.672
S tier for sure.

00:10:19.672 --> 00:10:22.589
(video game music)

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.380
Bobby Donnell from "The Practice".

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.670
Bobby Donnell, played by Dylan McDermott.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.550
Let's say, I don't know, C tier,

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:31.600
mainly on account of the
fact that Dylan McDermott

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.183
is not Dermot Mulroney.

00:10:34.025 --> 00:10:36.715
(video game music)

00:10:36.715 --> 00:10:38.820
Lionel Hutz from "The Simpsons".

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.910
Now, this is obviously
everyone's go-to punching bag

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.800
in terms of lawyers that
are terrible at their jobs.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.470
His own law firm is called I
Can't Believe It's A Law Firm,

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:50.990
and he doesn't appear to know
anything about the law itself.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.610
- Mr. Simpson, don't you worry.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.590
I watched "Matlock" in a bar last night.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.840
The sound wasn't on, but I
think I got the gist of it.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.110
- But there is an extremely
interesting wrinkle

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.270
to Lionel Hutz, and that is,

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.010
I don't think Lionel Hutz
has ever lost a case.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.340
He successfully represented
Bart in a copyright suit

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.710
regarding Itchy and Scratchy.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.730
He successfully represented
Homer in his case

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.600
against the restaurant
for unlimited shrimp,

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.520
the most egregious case
of fraudulent advertising

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:15.890
since the Never Ending Story.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.460
And he successfully
represented Homer again

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.140
in a case against the devil.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:22.500
Lionel Hutz is unstoppable.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.830
And the best part is, if
you don't win your case,

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.920
your pizza is free.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.140
- You'd be surprised how often that works.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:29.180
You really would.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:32.323
- So contrary to popular
belief, Lionel Hutz, A tier.

00:11:33.329 --> 00:11:36.460
(video game music)

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.470
The entire cast of "Ally McBeal".

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:41.608
Frankly, all of these lawyers
are basically interchangeable.

00:11:41.608 --> 00:11:44.870
Reasonable law skills, though
they couldn't help themselves

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.530
from just engaging in all kinds
of antics in the courtroom,

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.610
sometimes doing things that
would get you disbarred.

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.080
- Some even cheat.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.934
- Objection, move to strike!

00:11:53.934 --> 00:11:55.590
(cat hisses)

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.949
- So yeah, D tier.

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:00.700
(video game music)

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:02.670
Perry Mason from "Perry Mason",

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.520
and a whole bunch of other things.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:08.310
Perry Mason is the oldest
character in the entire build.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.440
None of these other characters

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.410
would exist without Perry Mason.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.070
He's the one that created the whole idea

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.040
of a TV fictional lawyer.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.130
Perry Mason is also extremely successful.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:21.780
Lawyer skills are above average, I'd say.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.680
Certainly no one can
dispute his results here.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.809
He almost always is able

00:12:25.809 --> 00:12:28.330
to successfully defend his clientele,

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.240
though he is, of course,

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.240
hampered by the eponymous
Perry Mason moment.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:33.590
- You didn't kill Thompson.

00:12:34.794 --> 00:12:37.211
But you did, Mr. Wells.

00:12:37.211 --> 00:12:38.170
- Yes!

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:40.004
Yes I killed Ned Thompson!

00:12:40.004 --> 00:12:41.230
I killed him!

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.200
I killed him, I killed him, I killed him!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.610
- When you have another
witness on the stand

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:48.274
and through a combination of lawyer skills

00:12:48.274 --> 00:12:50.810
and just straight up badgering,

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.600
you get them to confess to the crime

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.530
that your client is accused of.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:57.900
Now, anyone can represent
a client who is innocent.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.013
It takes real skill to represent someone

00:13:00.013 --> 00:13:03.000
who is clearly not innocent,
and Perry Mason benefits

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.170
from always having innocent clients.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.590
So Perry Mason really benefits

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:09.620
from his domino-like
special ability, luck.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.840
He's lucky in the clients
that he represents.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:15.140
He's lucky in that he's
able to elicit confessions

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.240
from basically everyone
except for his clients.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.060
That's not the way these things work.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:24.270
So despite being the
err TV fictional lawyer,

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.483
I'm gonna knock him down a peg, B tier.

00:13:27.644 --> 00:13:30.330
(video game music)

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.297
Ben Matlock from "Matlock".

00:13:32.297 --> 00:13:36.210
"Matlock" basically is just a
continuation of "Perry Mason".

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:39.310
It seems to be "Perry Mason",
except in the south, I guess?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.300
Matlock is ethical,
he's a straight shooter

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.140
and he's a hell of an investigator.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:46.260
Matlock is basically a Clefairy Pokemon

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:50.250
in that he is able to cast
his special ability, charm.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.640
Folksy, folksy, Southern charm.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.620
All in all, I'll give Matlock
one more than Perry Mason,

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.453
A tier.

00:13:58.351 --> 00:14:01.590
(video game music)

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.730
Marshall Eriksen from
"How I Met Your Mother".

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.354
Marshall is one of the few lawyers

00:14:05.354 --> 00:14:07.430
that we get to see grow up,

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.930
that we see him studying in law school,

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.280
we see him pass the BAR

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.290
and we see him enter the
world of private practice.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:15.500
Marshall is the main character

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.620
in one of the greatest episodes
about being a law student

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.310
being courted by the big firms,

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.960
where he's wined and dined by John Cho,

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:25.010
eats Kobe lobster, and
then does the walk of shame

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.950
after drinking far too much.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.570
- Much of what I do does not make me cry.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.360
- His lawyering skills are top-notch.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.490
He has several special abilities,

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:34.380
including the fact that
he can yell lawyered

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:35.730
when people have been lawyered.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.420
- Kaboom, you've been lawyered.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:39.850
- And of course, powerful slaps.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.330
- I'll let you slap me in
the face as hard as you can.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.657
- You have my attention.

00:14:42.657 --> 00:14:43.490
(slap connects)

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:45.210
- I don't really care
how you met your mother,

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.853
but Marshall Erickson is S tier, baby.

00:14:47.853 --> 00:14:51.245
(video game music)

00:14:51.245 --> 00:14:53.900
Harvey Birdman from "Harvey Bird Man".

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:57.930
Here, Harvey's lawyering
skills are mediocre at best.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:01.037
- Avenger, my personal digital assistant.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.313
Um, how do you make a T again?

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.520
Do you push that and then leave it down?

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:09.330
- He bats about a 500

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:11.190
when it comes to taking things to trial.

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:13.720
Usually the trial gets waylaid
by all the crazy things

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.720
that are happening as a result
of the superheroes involved.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.180
But his fighting abilities are top notch.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.530
He's powered by the sun,

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.050
he can shoot energy beams from his wrists,

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:25.380
he can create a solar powered shield,

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.070
and Harvey Birdman can fly.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.440
He's one of the main
attorneys at Seven and Seven,

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.180
the law firm, though it does appear

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:34.380
that he got his law degree
from a correspondence course,

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.810
which is never a good sign.

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:39.240
But even that can't take
away his power of attorney.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.643
The power of attorney!

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:42.483
C tier.

00:15:43.466 --> 00:15:46.913
(video game music)

00:15:46.913 --> 00:15:49.060
Jackie Chiles from "Seinfeld".

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.437
Clearly a stand in for Johnny Cochran,

00:15:51.437 --> 00:15:53.690
reasonably good lawyering skills.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:55.940
We covered this in A Real Lawyer Reacts.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.100
The problem is whenever
he represents Kramer,

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.317
he always loses and he
couldn't even defend the bunch

00:16:01.317 --> 00:16:04.230
from a law that doesn't actually exist.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.460
- Good Samaritan law?

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:06.750
You don't have to help anybody.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.280
That's what this country's all about.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.857
That's deplorable,
unfathomable, improbable.

00:16:10.857 --> 00:16:11.710
Hold on.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.010
- As we discussed in that episode,

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.820
there really aren't
any Good Samaritan laws

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.080
that require you to
affirmatively help out people

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.980
who have been injured in a crash.

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:21.220
So the fact that the entire Seinfeld gang

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:23.000
went to jail for over a year

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.590
doesn't bode well for Jackie Chiles.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.549
B tier at best.

00:16:27.549 --> 00:16:30.086
(video game music)

00:16:30.086 --> 00:16:32.210
Gerri Kellman from "Succession".

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:35.960
She is the general counsel
to Waystar Royco, feel it,

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:39.680
and she seems to know where
all of the bodies are buried.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.910
Gerri could very clearly run

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:43.090
the entire Waystar Royco company,

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.830
though she will absolutely
never be given that chance.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.860
She gives reasonably good legal advice,

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.300
whether it's a proxy war

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:52.050
or whether the entire
United States Congress

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:53.550
wants to come down on the company

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.010
as a result of what's going on in cruises.

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.720
- This may not be the best situation,

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:01.140
but there are harder jobs and
you get a (beep)load of cake.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:01.973
- Feel it.

00:17:01.973 --> 00:17:03.960
Her special abilities include opportunism

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.160
and whatever's going on
between her and Roman.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:09.520
If you've seen the show, you
know what I'm talking about.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.945
Gerri Kellman is just absolutely the best,

00:17:11.945 --> 00:17:14.770
but she's never going to
be given an opportunity

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:17.300
to get to the top, and the
same thing holds true here.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:20.516
A tier, misses out on on S tier.

00:17:20.516 --> 00:17:23.670
(video game music)

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.060
Jeff Winger from "Community".

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.590
