entire premise of the show

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:30.170
is that Jeff Winger is
not actually a lawyer,

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:33.620
so it's extremely tempting to
just DQ him from this list.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.840
- Are you a good person being
sued, oppressed or beaten?

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.690
I can help, and that's
the Winger guarantee.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.410
- Though if memory serves,
I guess in the last season,

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.520
he does actually get his BAR license back,

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.353
starts a private practice,

00:17:46.353 --> 00:17:50.000
then leaves to become a professor
at Greendale once again.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.330
But the thing is, any time
we actually see Jeff Winger

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.720
do something that is lawyer-like,

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.290
he tends to be pretty bad at it.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:57.910
- I discovered at a very early age

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.190
that if I talk long enough,

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.320
I could make anything right or wrong.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.260
So either I'm God or truth is relative,

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.800
and in either case, booyah.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.950
- Sometimes he's able
to convince the group

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:08.820
to do what he wants,

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.580
and sometimes they just
simply don't listen to him.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.830
So law skills are lacking.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.570
He doesn't appear to have any
special abilities whatsoever.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.501
D tier at best.

00:18:17.501 --> 00:18:20.017
(video game music)

00:18:20.017 --> 00:18:23.540
Alan Shore and Denny
Crane from "Boston Legal".

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.440
These guys are scumbags.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.400
They are womanizers, they're conniving,

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:28.810
and they are loathsome,

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:32.250
but their closing arguments
are the stuff of legends.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.510
There seems to be no rule
that they won't break

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.920
in order to get the right
result for their client.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.170
Look, sometimes you
want the scumbag lawyer.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:41.003
A tier.

00:18:41.868 --> 00:18:44.309
(video game music)

00:18:44.309 --> 00:18:46.660
Alicia Florrick, "The Good Wife".

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.920
Alicia here is able to do a great job

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.250
in navigating the
politics of law firm life,

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.820
which is not something that
you see all that often,

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.900
and she does a reasonably good
job in the courtroom as well.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.330
A little shaky at the start,

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.100
but eventually rises to the level

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.060
of equity partner in her firm.

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:04.660
So this was a close call,
but I'm going with B tier.

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:08.260
(video game music)

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:10.120
Jack McCoy from "Law and Order".

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.510
Here, Jack McCoy's lawyering skills

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.250
are absolutely unparalleled.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.960
Perhaps one of the most realistic,

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.540
but also just his pure
skill is unparalleled.

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:20.840
Given that his personal code

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.700
is that if there is a law out
there, he will enforce it,

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:26.730
he tends to skew towards lawful neutral.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:28.720
- Where there's a law, I'll enforce it.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:30.993
Where there's a crime, I'll prosecute it.

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:34.800
And where there's a victim,
I'll speak for that victim.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.140
That's my bottom line.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:38.150
- He's not about to use the legal system

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.530
for his own personal gain,

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.050
which leads him to being a civil servant,

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:44.950
a conduit through which
the law is administered

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.700
to the rest of society,

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.980
and through his hard work and dedication,

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.470
he eventually rises to the ranks

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:52.930
of actual district attorney for Manhattan.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:55.790
Special abilities
include enormous eyebrows

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.510
and a motorcycle, so,
you know, there's that.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:01.110
Jack McCoy easily makes S tier,

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:04.470
one of the best lawyers
in the entire build.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.464
Hands-down S tier, easy.

